## 1. The Big Idea

_This is the **Margin** poster. A single honest proportion bar opens it: **90% THE WORK** (program · diet · sleep — already built across Parts 1–3) versus **10% THE MARGIN** (everything in this article). That 10% slice is bracketed and exploded downward into a two-tier catalog. **Tier 1 — Natty** is an open shelf of four mechanism buckets (energy · cognition · fat-loss · pump/recovery), each compound carried as a mono spec row with its mechanism, dose, and timing. Below it sits a heavy **safety interlock** — three keys that must all be turned (bloodwork · a doctor who knows the protocol · a structured plan) — and only past that gate, in a visibly quarantined zone, the **Tier 2 — Half-Natty** transparency catalog (Retatrutide · CJC-1295+Ipamorelin · MK-677 · Clen/Cardarine), each labelled "shown, not recommended." A final **impact ladder** pins the priority order right-side-up, with the inverted "what most people optimize" version struck through beside it._ The poster is the spec sheet for the final 10% — and its whole job is to keep that 10% from being mistaken for the point.

## 2. Visual Metaphor & Structure

A **margin / trim-gain panel layered on a foundation block, feeding a two-zone gated catalog with a safety interlock.** The visual language is the engineering instrument that documents a *fine-adjustment stage*: a large fixed input (the foundation) whose magnitude is set elsewhere, a small trim band that this panel controls, and a catalog of adjustment modules — half of them open, half locked behind a hardware interlock. The honesty of proportion (small trim on a large foundation) and the physicality of the interlock (you must turn three keys) are the two semantic anchors.

The composition has five functional zones:

- **Zone 1 — The 90/10 margin bar (hero, top).** A single proportion bar showing **THE WORK · 90%** as one massive block and **THE MARGIN · 10%** as a thin terminal slice. The 90% block is annotated with the upstream parts (`Program · Part 3` / `Calorie phase · Part 1` / `Sleep & structure · Part 2`) so it reads as *already built, not theoretical*. A bracket on the 10% slice says "this article" and two thin rails explode that slice downward into the catalog. This bar is the first and loudest thing on the poster — the proportion is the argument.
- **Zone 2 — Tier 1 · NATTY (the open shelf).** Four mechanism-bucket modules laid in a clean grid: **ENERGY / CARDIO**, **PRE-WORKOUT COGNITION**, **FAT LOSS · cut-only**, **PUMP / RECOVERY**. Each module is a small instrument card with a bucket header and dense mono compound rows in the format `COMPOUND · mechanism · dose · timing`. State chips mark the cadence — `year-round`, `cut-only`, `cycle it` — so the reader sees not just *what* but *when*. This zone reads "open / go" — it's the tier the article says is appropriate for almost anyone serious.
- **Zone 3 — The safety interlock (full-width gate, the hard boundary).** A heavy horizontal interlock band separating Tier 1 from Tier 2 — drawn as a physical gate with **three keys that must all be turned** before it opens: `1 · COMPREHENSIVE BLOODWORK`, `2 · A DOCTOR WHO KNOWS WHAT'S BEING RUN`, `3 · A STRUCTURED PLAN (dose · duration · monitoring)`. A stamped label across the gate: `NOT A RECOMMENDATION GATE — A TRANSPARENCY GATE.` This is the poster's emotional pivot: everything above is open, everything below is locked and cautioned.
- **Zone 4 — Tier 2 · HALF-NATTY (the quarantined catalog).** Four compound cards in a visibly cordoned zone (danger chrome, hatched border): **RETATRUTIDE**, **CJC-1295 + IPAMORELIN**, **MK-677**, **CLENBUTEROL / CARDARINE**. Each card carries `mechanism · what it's actually for · the headline caveat` — never a dose protocol presented as a how-to. A persistent watermark/label on the zone: `SHOWN FOR TRANSPARENCY — NOT ENDORSEMENT.`
- **Zone 5 — The impact ladder (the un-invertible priority order).** A 5-rung vertical ladder pinned right-side-up: `1 Training stimulus & consistency` → `2 Calorie management` → `3 Sleep & recovery` → `4 Tier 1 supplements` → `5 Tier 2 compounds`. Beside it, a ghosted, struck-through "inverted" ladder labelled `WHAT MOST PEOPLE OPTIMIZE` (Tier 2 on top, fundamentals at the bottom) with a single correction arrow flipping it. This is where the article's "people get this backward" lands as geometry.

This sub-archetype — **margin bar + gated two-tier catalog + safety interlock + priority ladder** — is deliberately different from 3.3's dual-config datasheet, 3.1's single hero curve, and 3.2's vertical build-up, while remaining unmistakably "Engineering Diagnostic Instrument." Where the program posters showed *the machine being built and run*, this one shows *the trim stage you only touch after the machine is already running — and the locked drawer you mostly shouldn't open.*

